    User->>Page: choose category (idea/bug/general), write message (>= 10 chars)
    Page->>Fn: functions.invoke("feedback-submit", { message, category,<br/>context: { route, user_agent, submitted_at } })
    Note over Fn,Bucket: BACKEND IMPLEMENTATION UNKNOWN internals of the function itself,<br/>but the expected effect per FACTS.md is:
    Fn->>DB: insert feedback row (id, user_id, category, message, context, created_at)
    Fn->>Bucket: write a mirror object into feedback-messages (private, <uid>/... convention)
    alt function error or nothing recorded
        Fn-->>Page: error / { ok:false, database_recorded:false, storage_recorded:false }
        Page->>Log: trackFailure("feedback_submit_failed", { category, outcome })
        Page-->>User: error.submitFailedGeneric (typed text kept in the form)
    else partial (one leg recorded, e.g. HTTP 207)
        Fn-->>Page: { database_recorded xor storage_recorded }
        Page->>Log: trackFailure("feedback_submit_failed", { category, outcome: "partial" })
        Page-->>User: error.partial — retry, typed text kept in the form
    else full success
        Fn-->>Page: { ok:true, database_recorded:true, storage_recorded:true }
        Page->>Log: track("feedback_submitted", { category })
        Page-->>User: success toast + saved confirmation, form cleared
    end

    Admin--xDB: (expected) admin surface reads feedback rows
    Admin--xBucket: (expected) admin surface reads feedback-messages objects
    Note over Admin: BACKEND IMPLEMENTATION UNKNOWN — no admin retrieval UI or API<br/>is present in this frontend codebase; retrieval is inferred only.
